And that's probably not the best way to start out. Download a complete
development system, including editor, project manager, compiler and so
on. This will take all the trouble of where to put the system headers
and compiler, how to call the linker, how to tell the compiler where
your C files are, and all that kerfuffle, away from you, and put the
system itself neatly in one directory and let you arrange your projects
as you want them.
There are several free ones. I recommend Dev-C++ (which, despite the
name, also does C itself), for its straightforwardness and compactness;
or if you want something a bit more fully-featured (but also more
complex), Pelles C.

